</figure>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.20837v1/figures3/llm-comparison.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/185;" width="333" height="185" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A1.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per language comparison of unit test–based and LLM-based verification strategies. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.20837v1/synth_human_tests_correctness_overlap.svg" id="A1.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/159;" width="381" height="159"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A1.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sankey diagram representing the overlap and distribution of sample counts among two verification processes: Synthetic unit tests verification (pass/fail) and Expert-written unit tests (pass/fail), and the correctness of synthetic unit tests.</span></figcaption>
